<hr />

<h2 id="should-you-stay">Should You Stay on Draft2Digital or Switch?</h2>
<p>The answer depends on your publishing volume. Here is a simple decision framework:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>You earn over $100/year on Draft2Digital</strong> → The new fees do not affect you. The $20 activation fee applies only to new accounts. If you already have an account, you can stay without paying any yearly maintenance. Your effective cost is the 10-25% distribution commission, which may still be competitive depending on your store mix.</li>
<li><strong>You earn $30-99/year</strong> → The $12 annual fee eats 12-40% of your earnings. Consider switching to StreetLib (free setup, 18% commission) or directly uploading to Kobo Writing Life and Apple Books.</li>
<li><strong>You are a new author</strong> → Paying $20 upfront plus up to $24 in annual fees before you reach $100/year in sales means spending $44+ before your books are profitable. Start with StreetLib or Kobo Writing Life instead, and consider Draft2Digital only once you have established sales.</li>
</ul>
<hr />

<h2 id="how-to-export">How to Export Your EPUB Catalog from Draft2Digital</h2>
<p>If you decide to switch platforms, here is the step-by-step process to move your EPUB files out of Draft2Digital:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Log into your Draft2Digital dashboard</strong> and navigate to your book list.</li>
<li><strong>Download the EPUB master file</strong> for each title. Draft2Digital stores your original uploaded EPUB. Look for the "Download EPUB" or "Source Files" option in the book details menu.</li>
<li><strong>Validate each EPUB</strong> using the <a href="https://validator.w3.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">W3C EPUB Validator</a>. Draft2Digital may have modified your original file during the conversion process.</li>
<li><strong>Create accounts</strong> on your new platforms. We recommend starting with <a href="/blog/kobo-storygraph-integration-2026/">Kobo Writing Life</a> and StreetLib as the primary alternatives.</li>
<li><strong>Upload your EPUB files</strong> to each new platform. Set your metadata and pricing.</li>
<li><strong>Unpublish from Draft2Digital</strong> after confirming the new distribution is live. Draft2Digital does not charge a fee to unpublish books.</li>
</ol>
<p>Need to convert existing files to fresh EPUBs? Use <a href="/">converter-epub.com</a> to generate clean EPUB 3 files from DOCX, HTML, or Markdown source material.</p>
